WEBVTT

00:00:01.530 --> 00:00:01.610
Thank you.

00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:35.820
Ashi na mi wo soro etanji

00:01:35.850 --> 00:01:36.630
You have to leave us.

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:38.310
We're together to escape.

00:01:38.730 --> 00:01:40.710
You can't die, so leave us.

00:01:41.230 --> 00:01:47.060
I promise, I'll come back to free the thieves.

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:52.430
The thieves who attacked the government have already surrendered.

00:01:52.430 --> 00:01:53.390
And Rothgard?

00:01:53.670 --> 00:01:54.770
He escaped because of a bad luck.

00:01:55.870 --> 00:01:58.660
I'm Merian. Welcome to our planet Earth.

00:01:58.900 --> 00:01:59.920
Where did the planet come from?

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:06.420
Since I was born in Busan, my home has been turned into an impregnable empire by our powerful Emperor.

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:11.080
They have the ambition to take over the whole world, including your planet.

00:02:11.660 --> 00:02:16.340
I have noticed that your weapons are weak. You have no chance against the Bosnians.

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:21.560
That's why it's time for us to build a strong defense that will help you.

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:49.130
My poor child. I don't think he will ever get to know his father again.

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:52.970
Rosalia, don't say things like that.

00:02:52.970 --> 00:02:58.600
Until we find out the whereabouts of your husband and my child.

00:02:58.940 --> 00:02:59.900
Not anymore.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:02.740
We can say that Rothgard is dead.

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:05.500
He will come back to save us.

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:13.190
Yes, we will not be abandoned by your father.

00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:17.700
What will you name him?

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:28.300
Are you happy, my love?

00:03:33.930 --> 00:03:37.780
I'm more happy to be able to serve in the Bazaar.

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:43.510
I'm sure that tomorrow will be a good day for us to face our parents.

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:50.140
The next is the emperor of the Bazaar.

00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:51.950
The emperor already?

00:03:52.450 --> 00:03:55.130
I'm going to give birth early.

00:03:55.170 --> 00:03:58.380
How can a man become our son?

00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:01.620
I'm sure of it.

00:04:02.410 --> 00:04:04.660
And I've already prepared this.

00:04:04.900 --> 00:04:13.740
This is his very first weapon,

00:04:14.060 --> 00:04:20.120
that he will use as the saviour of the Empire.

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:26.420
An arrow that will break our family.

00:04:30.510 --> 00:04:31.850
Ang kambal na kalapati.

00:04:31.910 --> 00:04:40.140
Kay gandang regalo to para sa ating magiging anak.

00:04:56.600 --> 00:04:57.080
Sardos.

00:05:00.180 --> 00:05:00.840
Sardos.

00:05:02.890 --> 00:05:05.390
Sardos means strong.

00:05:06.980 --> 00:05:10.000
His name really suits him.

00:05:10.860 --> 00:05:15.430
Because this child will be our strength.

00:05:16.790 --> 00:05:18.540
Right, my father?

00:05:19.020 --> 00:05:19.440
Rosalia?

00:05:28.680 --> 00:05:29.120
Rosalia?

00:05:30.990 --> 00:05:32.210
Rosalia, don't look at him!

00:05:32.490 --> 00:05:33.670
Rosalia, fight him!

00:05:37.800 --> 00:05:38.340
Rosalia!

00:05:43.340 --> 00:05:43.880
Rosalia!

00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:49.870
Oh, my God!

00:05:52.810 --> 00:05:55.530
He's the only one I love!

00:06:18.720 --> 00:06:20.260
My wife is safe now.

00:06:23.460 --> 00:06:28.940
We're safe.

00:06:32.300 --> 00:06:32.760
I'm sorry.

00:06:33.080 --> 00:06:39.960
What can you do but start over?

00:06:40.990 --> 00:06:41.970
Rebuild yourself.

00:06:42.570 --> 00:06:45.580
Forget about the pain you've been through.

00:06:48.280 --> 00:06:52.870
Rosgar is dead.

00:06:52.990 --> 00:06:56.560
I'm just a vandal.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:01.940
A different person from here in your world.

00:07:02.100 --> 00:07:04.860
That's right!

00:07:06.140 --> 00:07:09.720
That's why we should change your name.

00:07:09.960 --> 00:07:12.080
For your new identity.

00:07:12.420 --> 00:07:14.720
What do you want as your new name?

00:07:14.940 --> 00:07:18.060
What do you think suits me?

00:07:23.390 --> 00:07:23.770
Do you like it?

00:07:23.940 --> 00:07:27.310
Do bullets not hit you?

00:07:34.640 --> 00:07:36.700
You survived and reached our planet.

00:07:37.140 --> 00:07:41.660
So your name should reflect that.

00:07:41.780 --> 00:07:45.000
It should also inspire people to listen.

00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:45.560
Arms!

00:08:01.440 --> 00:08:02.220
Ned Armstrong.

00:08:02.680 --> 00:08:09.010
Ned Armstrong.

00:08:09.410 --> 00:08:12.300
The name of my dead father is Ned.

00:08:12.600 --> 00:08:17.550
I'm sorry if I have to use it on you, but if you don't want to...

00:08:17.550 --> 00:08:21.500
I want a nice name.

00:08:21.720 --> 00:08:29.940
If I don't have one now, that's what I'll call him.

00:08:30.060 --> 00:08:34.090
I'm Ned Armstrong.

00:08:38.300 --> 00:08:39.900
That's why your name is new.

00:08:40.120 --> 00:08:44.090
We should also change your hair.

00:08:44.350 --> 00:08:46.500
You need to shave.

00:09:28.730 --> 00:09:29.830
I don't want to see my family.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:32.580
What is his name?

00:09:33.360 --> 00:09:33.880
Zardos.

00:09:34.700 --> 00:09:35.220
Zardos.

00:09:35.340 --> 00:09:38.380
The son of his father, Tridor.

00:09:38.720 --> 00:09:41.440
The real Tridor!

00:09:41.660 --> 00:09:46.320
Did you forget when I beat an old man?

00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:50.220
Mom, get the child.

00:09:51.150 --> 00:09:57.890
No. I can't do this.

00:10:01.310 --> 00:10:03.370
Don't take my father from me.

00:10:03.410 --> 00:10:04.910
I'm talking to myself.

00:10:04.910 --> 00:10:05.910
I'm in a daze.

00:10:06.290 --> 00:10:06.830
Don't!

00:10:07.640 --> 00:10:08.180
Don't!

00:10:08.400 --> 00:10:10.710
Fadza, don't worry.

00:10:12.200 --> 00:10:14.680
I will not allow you to go back to him.

00:10:51.850 --> 00:10:59.770
If we want to make a battle for our army, we need to build a defense against the ultimate weapon.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:03.040
of Bosan Najmi Berry.

00:11:03.260 --> 00:11:06.020
In your language, we call it

00:11:06.020 --> 00:11:11.260
The Beast Fighters

00:11:11.260 --> 00:11:14.760
are robots with artificial intelligence.

00:11:16.390 --> 00:11:17.810
They are strong, fast.

00:11:18.880 --> 00:11:21.620
They were made to destroy

00:11:22.600 --> 00:11:25.370
any enemy on our planet.

00:11:25.590 --> 00:11:29.970
We need...

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:33.820
We have to make our own fighting robot.

00:11:39.770 --> 00:11:44.890
Ned is a top scientist in Busan.

00:11:45.590 --> 00:11:48.150
And he knows the technology behind the Beast Fighters.

00:11:48.210 --> 00:11:54.060
With our help, he can engineer our own version of the Beast Fighters.

00:11:54.240 --> 00:11:58.120
Why do you plan to build this robot?

00:12:00.160 --> 00:12:01.140
An island would be ideal.

00:12:01.280 --> 00:12:07.000
An island where we can build a camp.

00:12:07.280 --> 00:12:13.900
And where we can test and develop our fighting skills against the Bosnians.

00:12:14.590 --> 00:12:15.650
And I know a perfect place.

00:12:18.320 --> 00:12:26.560
Lieutenant, Falcon Island.

00:12:39.240 --> 00:12:47.080
This will be our technical plans for our ultra-electromagnetic volt-in fighting machine.

00:12:47.300 --> 00:12:55.640
We call it Voltes.

00:12:56.150 --> 00:12:57.150
Voltes 5.

00:12:58.150 --> 00:12:58.790
Voltes 5?

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:04.420
Because of the five vehicles of war that build the robot.

00:13:04.620 --> 00:13:16.890
These five vehicles, when combined or vaulted in,

00:13:17.070 --> 00:13:25.700
can build a big fighting robot that will save the planet Earth.

00:13:44.750 --> 00:13:47.630
Voltes 5 Roomba, you have a great idea.

00:13:48.010 --> 00:13:53.100
I'm inspired by you.

00:13:53.220 --> 00:13:59.140
I mean, I'm inspired by...

00:14:00.060 --> 00:14:03.850
to people like you who are ready to fight for their world.

00:14:05.720 --> 00:14:11.540
That's really the reason why I want to help people like Dr. Smith,

00:14:11.760 --> 00:14:14.950
Mr. Robinson, the people here.

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:01.180
We love our beloved child.

00:15:01.780 --> 00:15:13.500
A good leader in our language.

00:15:16.190 --> 00:15:16.990
Steve N.

00:15:17.250 --> 00:15:21.830
Steven or Steve?

00:15:30.670 --> 00:15:31.750
Do you want to hold him?

00:15:32.540 --> 00:15:59.640
I promised you.

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:06.700
to you, your mother, and to you.

00:16:06.900 --> 00:16:13.410
I will make sure that

00:16:15.740 --> 00:16:17.140
nothing bad will happen to you.

00:17:11.130 --> 00:17:13.670
The robot of Voltes V.

00:17:13.790 --> 00:17:19.380
Who is he?

00:17:19.420 --> 00:17:19.760
Yes.

00:17:20.670 --> 00:17:25.340
Lieutenant Sumera, have you seen Dr. Armstrong?

00:17:26.350 --> 00:17:28.830
He's with Dr. Smith and Colonel Robinson.

00:17:29.300 --> 00:17:29.920
Okay, thank you.

00:17:30.320 --> 00:17:30.780
Come on, kids.

00:17:38.210 --> 00:17:41.460
Well, Ned, your ship is finally fixed.

00:17:41.700 --> 00:17:46.370
What are we going to use that spaceship for?

00:17:49.840 --> 00:17:52.420
This is what I'm going to use to get back what I promised.

00:17:55.690 --> 00:17:57.170
The promises I still need.

00:18:01.080 --> 00:18:01.940
What did you say, Nick?

00:18:04.390 --> 00:18:04.650
Bea.

00:18:04.910 --> 00:18:07.790
When are you planning to tell me what you're planning to tell me?

00:18:07.790 --> 00:18:08.770
When you're already in the area?

00:18:09.110 --> 00:18:10.650
When you've already left?

00:18:11.050 --> 00:18:25.500
Why are you asking?

00:18:25.740 --> 00:18:27.390
Leave us alone.

00:18:31.820 --> 00:18:33.180
Where are you going, Papa?

00:18:36.320 --> 00:18:37.020
Don't leave!

00:18:37.470 --> 00:18:38.570
Don't leave us!

00:18:58.350 --> 00:18:58.390
Bye!

00:19:00.320 --> 00:19:04.480
Not yet. Not yet.

00:19:04.860 --> 00:19:13.190
I will wait for your mother's children to see your brother first.

00:19:13.230 --> 00:19:20.390
But for now, we need to talk to your mother.

00:19:21.570 --> 00:19:22.890
Leave me alone, okay?

00:19:24.460 --> 00:19:29.580
Papa, can we just look at the robot in the other hall?

00:19:31.280 --> 00:19:31.960
Okay, go.

00:19:33.140 --> 00:19:48.490
Sorry, Marian.

00:19:48.830 --> 00:19:52.880
You're really back.

00:19:53.280 --> 00:19:59.860
Oh, I'm remembering the lyrics.

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:04.040
Until now, they are being forced and made to suffer.

00:20:04.280 --> 00:20:06.970
Planet Earth!

00:20:07.210 --> 00:20:11.690
They are already doing all of their defense systems.

00:20:11.990 --> 00:20:14.960
They are also fixing the safeguards.

00:20:15.040 --> 00:20:17.200
Richard and Oscar and I will be talking to each other.

00:20:17.220 --> 00:20:22.870
Your son!

00:20:23.430 --> 00:20:28.470
That's right.

00:20:31.020 --> 00:20:35.800
I love you. I love you, my children.

00:20:36.060 --> 00:20:40.100
I'll be back.

00:20:40.520 --> 00:20:49.700
No, I don't want to. I'm afraid something bad will happen to you.

00:20:50.140 --> 00:20:51.880
You're not leaving. Stay with us.

00:20:52.060 --> 00:20:56.110
Marian, nothing bad will happen to me.

00:20:56.270 --> 00:20:58.450
I promise you.

00:21:00.540 --> 00:21:04.750
I will come back to you and to our children. We will be together again.

00:21:05.070 --> 00:21:09.830
I don't want to continue anymore.

00:21:10.150 --> 00:21:13.270
Because you're leaving already.

00:21:30.830 --> 00:21:33.520
Next on Voltes 5 Legacy

00:21:33.520 --> 00:21:37.580
Prince Pizardo wants to show that he got a medal in his studies

00:21:37.580 --> 00:21:40.020
Don't imitate your father

00:21:40.020 --> 00:21:41.310
I'm not his father

00:21:41.310 --> 00:21:43.490
He's a traitor to the whole of Busan

00:21:43.840 --> 00:21:45.620
I love you, Mary Ann

00:21:45.620 --> 00:21:48.020
I still love our children

00:21:48.490 --> 00:21:51.340
Brother, throw that away! Throw it away!

00:21:55.030 --> 00:21:59.210
You have the initiative to be part of the EDF special program

00:22:00.920 --> 00:22:05.740
There's an army hiding Camp Big Falcon.

00:22:06.790 --> 00:22:07.210
It's right there.

00:22:07.490 --> 00:22:10.020
How many of you have seen this?

00:22:10.760 --> 00:22:11.220
Sir!

00:22:11.320 --> 00:22:11.820
Yes, sir!

00:22:12.080 --> 00:22:14.040
I would like to introduce to you...

00:22:16.940 --> 00:22:17.780
Voltes V!
